@startuml
title Simplified Sequence Diagram for /decrypt

actor Client
participant SecurityLayer
participant DecryptAPI
participant Controller
participant ValidationService
participant AuthService
participant DecryptFacade
participant DecryptService
participant KeyStoreHelper
participant ClientKeyRegistry

Client -> SecurityLayer : send HTTPS POST /decrypt
activate SecurityLayer

SecurityLayer -> DecryptAPI : forward request
activate DecryptAPI

DecryptAPI -> Controller : handle request
activate Controller

Controller -> ValidationService : validate request & JWT
activate ValidationService
ValidationService --> Controller : valid or reject
deactivate ValidationService

Controller -> AuthService : authorize decryption
activate AuthService
AuthService --> Controller : access granted or denied
deactivate AuthService

Controller -> DecryptFacade : process decryption
activate DecryptFacade

DecryptFacade -> DecryptService : perform decryption
activate DecryptService

DecryptService -> KeyStoreHelper : retrieve client key
KeyStoreHelper --> DecryptService : SecretKey

DecryptService -> ClientKeyRegistry : get IV for client
ClientKeyRegistry --> DecryptService : IV

DecryptService -> DecryptService : decrypt using AES-GCM

DecryptService --> DecryptFacade : DecryptResultModel
deactivate DecryptService

DecryptFacade --> Controller : HTTP 200 with DecryptResponse
deactivate DecryptFacade

Controller --> DecryptAPI : HTTP 200 with DecryptResponse
deactivate Controller

DecryptAPI --> SecurityLayer : HTTP 200 with DecryptResponse
deactivate DecryptAPI

SecurityLayer --> Client : HTTP 200 with DecryptResponse
deactivate SecurityLayer

@enduml
